    summary: "Type: Vessel | Class: Barge Wreck | Subclass: Wood\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a wood barge wreck, resting in 40 feet of water and measuring roughly 15 feet by 6 feet. The barge wreck rests upright on the lakebed, with sections of the hull missing or separated and portions of the internal structure exposed. Visible features include large squared structural timbers, parallel wooden deck planking, several upright wooden structural members with an unknown purpose, exposed framing, and a curved metal fitting attached near one of the timbers.\n\nPrior Research and Theories\nPreviously, Coastal Sensing & Survey had classified this target as LU10. Described as a small work barge.",
