    summary: "Type: Debris | Class: Man Made | Subclass: Mixed Materials\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as man-made debris, resting in 40 feet of water. The debris rests partially embedded in the lakebed and consists primarily of two large worked timber sections with attached metal and line components. Visible features include cut timber ends, a metal ring or eye fitting attached to the timber, and a length of rope or cable associated with the fitting. The worked timbers and attached hardware may indicate a previous structural or mooring-related use, though we are unable to determine the target’s original function.\n\nPrior Research and Theories\nPreviously, Coastal Sensing & Survey had classified this target as LU11. Described as a large tire and debris item.",
