    status: "recently-explored",
    tagline: "This target has been classified as a metal shipwreck, resting in 30 feet of water.",
    summary: "Type: Vessel | Class: Shipwreck | Subclass: Metal\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a metal shipwreck, resting in 30 feet of water. Much of the steel hull and wheelhouse structure remain intact. Visible features include rectangular wheelhouse window openings, a flat steel deck, several deck cleats, a large deck opening, a large six-spoke metal handwheel associated with deck machinery, and assorted piping and metal fittings.\n\nPrior Research and Theories\nPreviously, Coastal Sensing & Survey had classified this target as LU21. No additional narrative description has been confirmed from the available source material. Lake Union Virtual Museum had documented this target as a 30-foot steel workboat. Described as containing equipment that may indicate the vessel was used as a fireboat. They also link this wreck to DCS Films’ documentation of the DIT Boat, the same source associated with LU022; Shipwreck City confirmed that this target is LU021, a steel workboat, and that LUVM accidentally erred by placing LU021, fireboat, at this location.",
    summarySections: [{heading: "Shipwreck City Data", body: "This target has been classified as a metal shipwreck, resting in 30 feet of water. Much of the steel hull and wheelhouse structure remain intact. Visible features include rectangular wheelhouse window openings, a flat steel deck, several deck cleats, a large deck opening, a large six-spoke metal handwheel associated with deck machinery, and assorted piping and metal fittings."}, {heading: "Prior Research and Theories", body: "Previously, Coastal Sensing & Survey had classified this target as LU21. No additional narrative description has been confirmed from the available source material. Lake Union Virtual Museum had documented this target as a 30-foot steel workboat. Described as containing equipment that may indicate the vessel was used as a fireboat. They also link this wreck to DCS Films’ documentation of the DIT Boat, the same source associated with LU022; Shipwreck City confirmed that this target is LU021, a steel workboat, and that LUVM accidentally erred by placing LU021, fireboat, at this location."}],
