    summary: "Type: Debris | Class: Man Made | Subclass: Wood\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as man-made wooden debris, resting in 40 feet of water and measuring roughly 28 feet by 8.5 feet. The debris rests in a concentrated pile on the lakebed with logs lying across and alongside one another. Visible features include logs with flat, sawn ends, several lengths and loops of rope possibly associated with the timber, and additional wooden material extending through the site. Some of the rope appears to remain attached to or wrapped around individual logs. We are unable to determine whether all of the visible logs and rope belong to a single deposited pile or form part of a broader concentration of debris.\n\nPrior Research and Theories\nPreviously, Coastal Sensing & Survey had classified this target as LU25. Described as a pile of logs. DCS Films had classified this target as a pile of logs and are described with dimensions of approximately 25 feet by 30 feet.",
