    coordinates: [47.6310925, -122.3281916],
    location: "Lake Union, Seattle",
    status: "recently-explored",
    tagline: "This target has been classified as a metal car wreck, resting in 15 feet of water.",
    summary: "Type: Vessel | Class: Car Wreck | Subclass: Metal\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a metal car wreck, resting in 15 feet of water. No overall dimensions are currently recorded for the target. During Shipwreck City’s updated survey, the previously documented Harley-Davidson motorcycle was not located. The site currently consists of an electric bicycle and scattered debris resting on the lakebed. Visible features include the electric bicycle, a barrel, and a smaller cylindrical object. We are unable to determine whether these objects are associated with the previously documented motorcycle site.\n\nPrior Research and Theories\nPreviously, Coastal Sensing & Survey had classified this target as LU66. Described as a Harley-Davidson motorcycle and noted that SDOT claimed it would be removed as part of the Eastlake Way Bridge project. DCS Films had classified this target as Target 25. Described as a Harley-Davidson motorcycle.\n\nAdditional Context\nCoastal Sensing & Survey reported that SDOT planned to remove the Harley-Davidson motorcycle as part of the Eastlake Way Bridge project. Shipwreck City’s later survey did not locate the motorcycle, making removal as part of the project a likely explanation.",
    summarySections: [{heading: "Shipwreck City Data", body: "This target has been classified as a metal car wreck, resting in 15 feet of water. No overall dimensions are currently recorded for the target. During Shipwreck City’s updated survey, the previously documented Harley-Davidson motorcycle was not located. The site currently consists of an electric bicycle and scattered debris resting on the lakebed. Visible features include the electric bicycle, a barrel, and a smaller cylindrical object. We are unable to determine whether these objects are associated with the previously documented motorcycle site."}, {heading: "Prior Research and Theories", body: "Previously, Coastal Sensing & Survey had classified this target as LU66. Described as a Harley-Davidson motorcycle and noted that SDOT claimed it would be removed as part of the Eastlake Way Bridge project. DCS Films had classified this target as Target 25. Described as a Harley-Davidson motorcycle."}, {heading: "Additional Context", body: "Coastal Sensing & Survey reported that SDOT planned to remove the Harley-Davidson motorcycle as part of the Eastlake Way Bridge project. Shipwreck City’s later survey did not locate the motorcycle, making removal as part of the project a likely explanation."}],
