    tagline: "This target has been classified as man-made wood debris, resting in 40 feet of water.",
    summary: "Type: Debris | Class: Man Made | Subclass: Wood\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as man-made wood debris, resting in 40 feet of water. The target lies flat against the lakebed and consists primarily of two long rectangular cut wooden members positioned side by side and appearing to be connected. Visible features include smaller metal fittings or fasteners attached along the outside of the wood and a length of rope or line that appears to be connected to the wooden assembly. Additional debris nearby includes a metal pipe, though we are unable to determine whether it is associated with the target. We are unable to determine the original purpose of the wooden structure from the available evidence.\n\nPrior Research and Theories\nPreviously, Coastal Sensing & Survey had classified this target as LU75. Described as an unknown target.",
