    summary: "Type: Vessel | Class: Shipwreck | Subclass: Wood\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a wood shipwreck, resting in 40 feet of water and measuring roughly 15 feet by 6 feet. The wood shipwreck rests upright and retains much of its overall hull form. Visible features include gunwales, outer and interior hull planking, several transverse wooden beams that appear to be thwarts or bench supports. Loose unidentifiable debris is visible within the hull.\n\nPrior Research and Theories\nPreviously, Coastal Sensing & Survey had classified this target as LU95. Described as one of two row boats located in an area of the lake containing dumped debris and cable.",
