    tagline: "This target has been classified as a mixed materials shipwreck, resting in 23 feet of water and measuring roughly 24 feet by 8 feet.",
    summary: "Type: Vessel | Class: Shipwreck | Subclass: Mixed Materials\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a mixed materials shipwreck, resting in 23 feet of water and measuring roughly 24 feet by 8 feet. The vessel sits upright on the lakebed, though much of the upper structure has collapsed or is missing, leaving the interior exposed. Visible features include the broad fiberglass hull, a raised cabin with several rectangular window openings, surviving sections of metal railing, a cleat and additional latches, fittings, and attachment hardware along the hull and deck. A projecting metal component near one end of the vessel is presumed to be an anchor, though its configuration is partially obscured by growth. The surviving cabin arrangement and overall hull form are consistent with a small cruising or recreational vessel, though the vessel's make, model, and identity have not yet been established.\n\nPrior Research and Theories\nNo prior documentation from Coastal Sensing & Survey, DCS Films, or the Lake Union Virtual Museum has been identified for this target.",
