    summary: "Type: Vessel | Class: Shipwreck | Subclass: Fiberglass\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a fiberglass shipwreck. Its depth and dimensions have not yet been confirmed in the current master record. The vessel remains largely intact and appears to rest upright or at a slight angle, with much of the hull and raised cabin structure still recognizable. Much of the exterior is covered by aquatic growth and encrustation. Visible features include the broad fiberglass hull, a raised cabin or deckhouse with several rectangular window openings, surviving sections of metal railing, and additional metal fittings attached around the deck and hull. A projecting metal component is visible near one end of the vessel, though its exact function cannot currently be determined. The surviving cabin arrangement and overall hull form are consistent with a small cruising or recreational vessel, though the vessel's make, model, and identity have not yet been established.\n\nPrior Research and Theories\nNo prior documentation from Coastal Sensing & Survey, DCS Films, or the Lake Union Virtual Museum has currently been identified for this target.",
