    summary: "Type: Vessel | Class: Shipwreck | Subclass: Wood\nShipwreck City Data\nThis target has been classified as a wood shipwreck. Its depth and dimensions have not yet been determined. The wreck rests low on the lakebed, with portions of the hull remaining upright while other sections have collapsed outward or separated from the main structure. Visible features include extensive outer hull planking, exposed internal framing, substantial transverse and longitudinal structural timbers, a heavy squared structural member at one end of the hull, and a two-horned fitting mounted near the upper edge of the bow. Several areas of planking have separated from the hull, exposing additional framing, while detached wooden material and other debris are scattered immediately around the wreck. \n\nPrior Research and Theories\nNo corresponding prior documentation from Coastal Sensing & Survey, DCS Films, or the Lake Union Virtual Museum has been identified for this target in the material reviewed to date.",
